[[7201,2771,"the Discharge procedure followed in respect of Mr. Watts' discharge from the Princess Royal Hospital in Haywards Heath, West Sussex on the 4\" December 2014 was deeply flawed. There was no ongoing process of discharge.","discharge procedure flaws",""],[7202,2771,"The discharge paperwork was effectively blank.","blank discharge paperwork",""],[7203,2771,"There was no communication as to the discharge, either with regard to the anticipated date of discharge or with the Nursing Home who were expected to receive him back or with Graham Watts' son. He was medically unfit for discharge arriving back at his Nursing Home hypothermic, hypotensive, oedematous and sleepy.","lack of discharge communication",""],[7204,2771,"It is acknowledged and accepted that a change of environment increases the risks of fall.","environment change fall risk",""],[7205,2771,"Evidence was heard to the effect that if Mr. Watts had not fractured his hip when he fell, he would not have died when he did.","hip fracture leading to death",""]]